## Session 50 summary

**Major breakthrough: root-caused and fixed the directory-dirent RESURRECTION** (the 90-session `tcp_dlm_scaling`/`dlm_fairness` "durable leftover dirent" blocker family).

**Root (PROVEN, RULE 4):** Not a DLM double-grant (refuted: `P106-STALE-EX`=0, `P-DOUBLEGRANT`=0, request-path already re-affirms, `purge_stale` is dead code). The real cause is the **cached-EX FAST-PATH `sf` 3-way merge** re-adding the node's **own** async-destaged-then-removed shortform dirent. I proved it with a new slow-path probe (`sfm_dbg` → `P-SFM-READD`): the leftover (`n1_i2_r119`→ino132) is re-added at `state=CACHED, peer_mod=0` — i.e. while the node holds the grant continuously (no peer could have modified). xfsaild async-destages an intermediate create; the node removes it in-core; the fast-path merge sees it on disk (`!ours !base`) and mis-classifies the node's own entry as a peer-add.

**Fix B (KEEP, build `E67385C9`):** on a continuous-hold fast path the in-core fork is authoritative — don't adopt lagging disk. One-line gate at `xfs_mxfs_dlm.c:9018` (`mxfs_sf_fastpath_adopt`, default 0 = fixed). Correct by construction; verified fast-path re-adds dropped to 0/0.

**Validation:** full `./run.sh 2 tcp` = **17/17 once** with Fix B.

**Criterion NOT yet met.** Reliability run 1 (clean reboot+reformat) then FAILED `tcp_dlm_scaling` on a **different residual: SLOWNESS/stall** — `got=45/150 rounds, >60s window, both nodes`. Diagnosis: a single dir-EX/AG-DLM handoff stalls (the acquire retries 60×1s=60s in `dlm_lock_impl`), blowing the window. This is the sess13/sess33 **cross-resource dir-EX↔AG-DLM distributed-deadlock** / lost-message family, worse in-suite (tcp_dlm_scaling runs last, contaminated LUN). Standalone passes.

**Next session:** read `/tmp/relrun_{1,2,3}.log` for stall consistency; reproduce the in-suite stall and instrument any DLM acquire taking >2s (seconds-scale = instrumentable, unlike the µs resurrection); fix the handoff stall root. Full diagnosis + fix direction saved in ccmemory `sess50-ROOT-resurrection-is-fastpath-sfmerge-readd-FIX-B`. Build `E67385C9` (Fix B) deployed on both nodes.

I did not write the criteria-met marker — the 2-node tcp suite is not yet reliably 100% (the handoff-stall residual remains).

